  "description": "One operation atomically reserves the portable 2359296-byte request, response, and parser-scratch set and converts request workspace to an exact retained 1 MiB request. A concurrent operation cannot acquire another complete set from the 4 MiB minimum and fails before observer/configuration/hooks/serialization/network with OVERLOADED/NOT_SENT and no partial byte acquisition. Releasing the held operation and then admitting an exact-1 MiB request plus exact-1 MiB response proves response/parser reservations have no post-publication rejection and all permits are reusable.",
